CORE
main.c
--refine-arrays --no-bounds-check
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ a\[1\] and b\[1\] may differ: FAILURE$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ a and b may be equal: FAILURE$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
--
^warning: ignoring
isEliminated
--
Checking all properties requires more than one solver call. Post-processing,
which adds the array constraints, must only be done once: repeating it added
constraints referring to variables that MiniSat's simplifier had eliminated
after the first call, which failed an assertion in MiniSat.
